          "heading": true
        },
        {
          "term": "quantum systems",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "\\label{sec:framework} Quantum systems, here the conduction electron gas, are made up of entities that occupy discrete states. These discrete levels are modified in an excited state such as a plasmon. As extreme plasmons are sustained by strong excitation of quantum electron gas, the statistical distribution of electron states significantly diverges from the initial Fermi-Dirac statistics, making linear theory",
      "extractCut": true
    },
